            0.621,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. In a museum, a woman walks towards a large concave mirror (Fig. 10.26). She will see that: (i) her erect image keeps decreasing in size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.693,
            0.621,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) her inverted image keeps decreasing in size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.715,
            0.621,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) her inverted image keeps increasing in size and eventually it becomes erect and magnified."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.774,
            0.594,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) her erect image keeps increasing in size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.801,
            0.622,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Hold a magnifying glass over text and identify the distance where you can see the text bigger than they are written. Now move it away"
